<ContentPage
  pageKey="temoignages"
  title="Testimonials"
  heading="Testimony of Damien Lefebvre"
  description="The path of Damien Lefebvre, from the DUT Computer Science at the IUT of Villetaneuse to his position as analyst-programmer in a French IT service company."
>
  <figure class="portrait">
    <Image src={portrait} alt="Portrait of Damien Lefebvre" width={178} height={209} />
    <figcaption>Damien Lefebvre, analyst-programmer</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <p>
    With his baccalaureate S in his pocket, Damien Lefebvre spent a few months at university before
    reorienting himself in search of a more structured training. His academic experience having
    revealed to him a taste for computing, he decided to apply to the IUT of Villetaneuse to prepare
    a DUT Computer Science, Software Engineering option, in 2002.
  </p>
  <p>
    The supervision provided by passionate professors and the acquisition of rigorous working
    methods encouraged him to complete his training with the Professional Licence in Computer
    Systems and Software, Software Engineering option, offered by the same IUT.
  </p>
  <blockquote>
    <p>
      “The knowledge and skills developed over three years of studying algorithmics and databases,
      but also the accounting aspects of the business world, were the key that allowed me to be
      recruited by a large French IT service company, after a 4-month end-of-year internship.”
    </p>
  </blockquote>
  <p>
    For a year and a half now, the young Analyst-Programmer has been putting his skills to the
    service of major customers, among which are renowned banking institutions, and in the future
    wishes to move towards “Consulting”.
  </p>
</ContentPage>
